# KVM inotify handoff

Draft pull request: https://github.com/rrnewton/reverie/pull/540

Exact published head: `ad140f072569a2ba6ad0bb11d3364c8e10c5db46`

The branch implements `inotify_init`, `inotify_init1`, `inotify_add_watch`, and
`inotify_rm_watch` in the KVM executor. It is draft, unmerged, and carries the
`post-facto-human-review` label. All source review markers name PR 540.

Exact-head checks:

- `cargo test -p reverie-kvm`: 262 passed, 0 failed.
- `cargo clippy -p reverie-kvm --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`: passed.
- Four intentional mutations were rejected by direct tests.

A precommit adversarial review found and then approved the repair for
descendant guest descriptor aliases. The test forces guest fd 5 to map to a
host fd at or above 100 and covers all four supported aliases.

A post-repair `cargo test --workspace --all-features` rerun reached the existing
`reverie_process::container::tests::pin_affinity_to_all_cores` test without an
earlier failure, then made no progress for 16 minutes and was stopped. A full
workspace run had passed before the final descriptor-alias repair.

Do not merge from this implementation slot. Independent exact-head human
review and downstream Hermit pin/cell validation remain.

## Local review repairs (not published)

The three findings from the independent review of published head
`ad140f072569a2ba6ad0bb11d3364c8e10c5db46` are repaired locally:

- nonzero move cookies are numbered from one per inotify open file
  description and stay shared through read/readv, dup/fcntl duplication,
  fork, and CLONE_FILES;
- watch paths accept `/dev/fd`, `/proc/self/fd`, `/proc/thread-self/fd`, and
  numeric current-pid/current-tid aliases while refusing direct or
  symlink-mediated access to supervisor procfs;
- CLONE_FILES executors release their private host descriptor copies after
  each syscall, so an idle worker cannot postpone last-close effects.

The repair is local commit
`68d6e294f16005a50ec4a0ffc082cbae085ce507`, one commit ahead of the published
pull-request head. It has not been pushed.

Exact-head checks:

- `cargo test -p reverie-kvm`: 266 passed, 0 failed.
- `cargo clippy -p reverie-kvm --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`: passed.
- `git diff ad140f072569a2ba6ad0bb11d3364c8e10c5db46 --check`: passed.
- Three review-finding mutations were rejected: raw host move cookies failed
  the two-run KVM test; removing numeric worker-TID alias handling failed the
  direct path test; retaining the worker snapshot after a completed syscall
  failed the threaded close-event test.

An inotify descriptor received without its cookie state (for example through
SCM_RIGHTS) fails reads with EOPNOTSUPP. Ordering remains limited to events
generated by the serialized guest workload; concurrent external filesystem
activity is not claimed deterministic. Do not push without coordinator authorization.
